#: ../../../variable/CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS.rst:2
msgid "CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS.rst:6
msgid ""
"Enable automatic generation and installation of Software Bill of Materials "
"(SBOM) documents for the project's install export sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS.rst:9
msgid ""
"Set this variable in the top-level directory, or in the cache, to ``spdx`` "
"to generate an SBOM for each export set created by :command:"
"`install(TARGETS)` with the ``EXPORT`` option.  Export sets already covered "
"by an explicit :command:`install(SBOM)` call are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS.rst:14
msgid ""
"Each automatically generated SBOM uses the export set name as its package "
"name and the top-level project name to obtain project metadata.  It is "
"installed under ``<libdir>/sbom/<export-name>``, where ``<libdir>`` is the "
"value of ``CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR``, or ``lib`` if that variable is unset or "
"empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS.rst:20
msgid ""
"The value uses the same format names as the ``FORMAT`` option of :command:"
"`install(SBOM)` and :command:`export(SBOM)`.  Currently, ``spdx`` and "
"``spdx-3.0+json`` are supported and select SPDX JSON output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS.rst:24
msgid ""
"For example, a package distributor can enable SBOM installation without "
"modifying a project's build scripts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS.rst:27
msgid ""
"cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS=spdx\n"
"cmake --build build\n"
"cmake --install build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../variable/CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS.rst:33
msgid ""
"Projects that need to customize SBOM metadata, format, or destination should "
"use :command:`install(SBOM)` directly."
msgstr ""
